    "field": "Integrated assessment modeling",
    "problem": "Narrow, sectoral assessments of coastal delta vulnerability fail to capture the complex interactions between climatic and socio-economic drivers, hindering evidence-based planning and prioritization by making it difficult to understand their relative importance for sustainable development.",
    "method": "This study uses a bespoke integrated assessment model (IAM), coupling biophysical and socio-economic models, to simulate future scenarios and assess the sensitivity of rural coastal Bangladesh to climate change and policy decisions.",
    "task": "The task is to analyze the relative importance of climate change versus socio-environmental development drivers on the future of rural coastal Bangladesh to 2050 using a bespoke integrated assessment model.",
